# MEGALIGHTS-NORT: Shadows Stochastic (MegaLights: ReSTIR DI samples, one visibility test each) on a device WITHOUT ray query. The method is no longer lowered for want of rays; its visibility source is (Common::Scalability::StochasticVisibility): rayquery -> vsm+screen (the screen trace over the closest HZB, then the light's VSM-LOCAL pages) -> screen. machine.json HideRayTracing=true hides the ray query; the device still has fragment stores and the 16k render area, so the source is vsm+screen.
# Headless shots, F:/BistroFoliageProj, machine.json {"HideRayTracing": true}, Shadows.Method Stochastic (3) overridden in machine.json.
Дано: F:/BistroFoliageProj, GI_Bistro_Night, machine.json HideRayTracing=true, Lit, camera on the street under the lamps.
Когда: run Quality "Quality: Shadows.Method Stochastic"; render 120 frames; state render,log
Тогда [megalights_nort] 0_night_stochastic_nort: state render.shadows.method == "Stochastic" (requested Stochastic, NOT lowered to CascadedMaps; no "[RenderMethods] Shadows:" lowering line in engine_log), render.shadows.visibility == "vsm+screen"; 0 VUID in engine_log; 0 error lines in engine_log (no "MegaLights:" line at all: "MegaLights: Volume" runs its MegaLightsVolumeVirtual program, froxels shadowed by the local lights' VSM-LOCAL pages); translucent glass lit by local lights: the Bistro window glass under a lamp is brighter than the same glass in a Shadows.Method Stochastic shot with the lamps disabled (pixel-diff over the glass region, mean > 0), and the engine_log/pass list has "MegaLights: Volume"; every local light casts a shadow: each lamp's pool on the pavement has the shadow of the poles/chairs/tables in it (pixel-diff against a Shadows.Method VirtualMaps shot of the same camera: the shadow shapes coincide), and the frame mean is not black (frame mean > the VirtualMaps shot's mean * 0.8).
Тогда [megalights_nort_vsm] 0_night_stochastic_nort: state render.shadows {method "Stochastic", visibility "vsm+screen"}; the pass list has "VSM: Raster Local <light> V<view> M<mip>" passes (the lamps' casters drawn into their pages for Stochastic too; the night scene has no sun, so no "VSM: Cull Casters L<n>"/"VSM: Raster L<n>" - a day shot of the same mode has both, SunShadowIsVirtual) and the composite draws "DeferredLighting MegaLights" (the screen-mask program with DESERT_MEGALIGHTS); lamp shadows soften with distance from the caster (VsmLocalVisibilityRay, SMRT along the sampled source-sphere direction): a chair leg's shadow is sharp where it meets the pavement and its penumbra widens away from the leg (edge width measured across the shadow at the foot and 50 cm out, the far one wider); 0 VUID, 0 error lines in engine_log.
Когда: run Quality "Quality: Shadows.Method Level"
Тогда 1_level override removed (machine.json clean of Shadows.Method).
